# Generated from the zod schema in
# `packages/agent/src/works-config/schema/works-config.schema.ts` and
# committed so it can be served without a build step. Its formatting is
# owned by `serializeWorksConfigJsonSchema()` — a drift test asserts the
# file is byte-identical to a fresh generation, so letting Prettier
# reformat it would fail that test on every run.
packages/agent/src/works-config/schema/works.v2.schema.json

# The same rule for the stand-alone App spec schema (APW-03 T8): generated by
# `serializeAppSpecJsonSchema()`, committed, and drift-guarded against a fresh
# generation. Prettier's JSON printer collapses short arrays and objects, so
# reformatting it would fail that guard on every run.
packages/agent/src/works-config/schema/app-spec.v1.schema.json

# Generated OpenAPI artifact (pnpm generate:openapi)
apps/api/openapi.json

# Agent Plugins conformance fixtures. These are deliberately malformed
# packages — invalid JSON, broken YAML frontmatter, over-length fields — and
# they ARE the test cases. The root format glob covers
# `**/*.{ts,tsx,jsx,json,css,md}`, so without this entry `format:check` fails
# on them in CI and `pnpm format` silently repairs them into valid documents,
# deleting the coverage. See packages/agent-plugins/fixtures/README.md.
packages/agent-plugins/fixtures

# Vendored canonical JSON Schemas for the Agent Plugins standard, copied
# verbatim from github.com/agentplugins/agent-plugins-spec so a diff here
# always means the upstream artifact changed. Reformatting them would make
# that comparison lie.
packages/agent-plugins/src/schemas

# In-product manual catalog (AW-25), generated from docs/ by
# `apps/web/scripts/build-help-catalog.mjs`. Its formatting is owned by the
# generator — `help-catalog.unit.spec.ts` asserts the file is byte-identical to
# a fresh generation, so letting Prettier reformat it would fail that test.
apps/web/src/lib/help/help-catalog.generated.ts

# The same generated JSON, one level further out: `build-help-catalog.mjs` also
# writes the per-page catalog data the web app serves, and `apps/web/.gitignore`
# already ignores the directory (`/public/help-content/`). A clean CI checkout has
# no such files, so this entry only stops a LOCAL `pnpm format:check` from
# reporting 25 phantom failures — the mirror image of the entry above.
apps/web/public/help-content

# App Works build artifacts (APW-13's golden-outputs work). This is the SAME rule
# as `app-spec.v1.schema.json` above, applied to the files that were missed:
# `_build-artifacts/apw-03-schema/app-spec.schema.json` is emitted by the same kind
# of serializer, and `_build-artifacts/expected-outputs/golden/README.md:340`
# records a **sha256 per file** (`app-spec.schema.json | 459fb280214f133a | 2090`)
# which `golden/check.mjs` verifies. Prettier rewrites the schema wholesale — 3 897
# lines — and rewriting the pinned files would fail that check on every run, so
# `--write` here is not a formatting fix, it is a broken golden. These four files
# are what the branch's FIRST CI run failed `Check formatting` on
# (`35393016450`, `lint-and-test (22.x)`, 11 files of which 7 were formatted and
# these 4 were not, deliberately).
docs/specs/features/app-works/_build-artifacts/apw-03-schema/app-spec.schema.json
docs/specs/features/app-works/_build-artifacts/templates-catalog/ever-works-templates/schema/templates-manifest.schema.json
docs/specs/features/app-works/_build-artifacts/expected-outputs/golden/.generated-files.json
docs/specs/features/app-works/_build-artifacts/expected-outputs/golden/__negative-control__/.variants.json
